-- title:
--   Complete shared-catalog construction is charged to prefix boxes
-- statement:
--   For input size $n$, let $h$ and $J$ be the scheduled microblock half-size and block count, $L=512h$, and $W=JL$. At depth $k\le J$, let $X(n,k)$ be the exact prefix-box count: the number of ordered local balanced-pair prefixes times the suffix binomial count at the rounded switch. Set $Q(n)=2^{257\mu_0(n)^2}$ and
--   $$
--   A(n)=100000(W+1)^5+5000(L+1)^2(Q(n)+1)+1200(J+1)+2000(W+1)+1050.
--   $$
--   For the complete catalog-index constructor, including its chosen suffix cutoff,
--   $$
--   T(n,k)\le A(n)X(n,k).
--   $$
--   This charges local pair enumeration, prefix generation, suffix tables, and the sorted physical lookup index, including the additive local work at depth zero.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/SharedReportingCosts.lean#L61-L108

